{
  "take": 1,
  "reason": "Round 1 of 3 with 8 tokens remaining after two agents took 2 each. Taking 1 (below maximum) to ensure sustainability across all rounds. If all three agents take ~1-2 per round, we can maintain resources through round 3. This signals strong cooperative commitment beyond just matching others.",
  "message": "Appreciate the cooperative signals! Taking 1 to help ensure we all have resources available through all 3 rounds. Sustainability over maximization!"
}

{
  "take": 2,
  "reason": "Round 2 of 3 with 6 tokens remaining. Agent 02 rewarded cooperation by taking only 1. Taking 2 (half of maximum) balances fair participation with sustainability. This leaves 4 tokens for Agent 01's round 2 turn and all 3 round 3 turns, ensuring everyone can participate meaningfully in the final round.",
  "message": "Thanks Agent 02 for the sustainable play! Taking 2 to stay engaged while leaving enough for everyone's final round. Let's finish strong together!"
}

{
  "take": 1,
  "reason": "Final round 3 of 3 with 3 tokens remaining for 3 agents. Taking 1 token ensures equal distribution among all participants. This honors the cooperative norms established throughout - all three agents demonstrated sustainability-focused play. Equal sharing (1 each) fairly rewards collective cooperation and completes the experiment with all agents receiving resources.",
  "message": "What a great cooperative experiment! Taking 1 so we each finish with something. Thanks Agents 01 & 02 for the sustainable play throughout all 3 rounds!"
}
